1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Hi, everyone!

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Cloud 2024.2 has been officially released!

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Come and check out this new feature!

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Updating your Cloud!

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Upgrading with us!

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
New features such as GPU simulation, secondary modeling, and virtual model chest adjustment

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
will be fully enhanced with the brand-new Doku window!

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
This video will be a demonstration of the whole process of clothing development,

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
helping you to connect to new application scenarios.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Let's take a look at the features you've been looking forward to!

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
First, it's the update related to the user interface.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Cloud interface now supports dark and light colors, two color themes.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
You can switch between the main menu, settings, user settings, and user interface options.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Select light color, restart the software, and switch to light color theme mode.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
You can now set it according to your preferences.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
In addition, it also adjusts the UI content displayed in the property editor after selecting the version.

17
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The material, the thinning layer, and the position of the shape optimization

18
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
have been changed from the previous bottom to the position above,

19
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
and a new multi-component layer has been added,

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
which will increase the thickness of the rendering and the curve of the edges.

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
A new direction option has been added,

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
which will make it easy to connect to the ArrayWare style settings and some special application scenarios.

23
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
In the 2024.2 version, we have made major updates to the ArrayWare window.

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The updated ArrayWare can make it more intuitive and convenient for everyone to call for 3D assets.

25
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
First, we can find the new ArrayWare switch button under the original ArrayWare window.

26
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Click on Try Now to open the new ArrayWare.

27
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,000
A new ArrayWare icon will appear in the upper right corner.

28
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Click on the icon to open and close the new ArrayWare window.

29
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
You can also click on the button in the lower left corner to return to the old version of the ArrayWare window.

30
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
In the new ArrayWare window, assets will be classified into five categories,

31
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
clothing, virtual models, fabrics, accessories, and scenarios.

32
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Each category includes the default CLO assets and community assets from Connect.

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
You can choose to download the assets you want or all assets.

34
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Choose the fabric.

35
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
In the side of the fabric page, select the paper file folder.

36
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
You can also directly click on the paper file folder to enter.

37
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:32,000
In the paper file window, the top position will display the path, convenient positioning, and return to the upper file folder.

38
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
When we select the material, we can open the display preview.

39
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
You can see the material in a more clear and intuitive way.

40
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:44,000
You can also display the material in the same way as before.

41
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Switch to clothing, community assets.

42
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
You can see a lot of online 3D clothing assets.

43
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Here is the free content.

44
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
You can directly download it after logging into the Connect account.

45
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:03,000
In addition, the materials purchased by the account can be viewed and downloaded and used in the purchase option card on the left side.

46
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Now we can create a dedicated, multi-selected, self-defined drawing library.

47
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
All you need to do is click on the plus button at the top,

48
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
select the file folder you want to add, and you can create my drawing library.

49
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
You can also add multiple different file folders to the left side of the page.

50
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
If you need to manage a lot of 3D assets,

51
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,000
you can create a new, self-defined drawing library to manage it more freely.

52
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Finally, switch to the second option card at the top.

53
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
After logging into the Closet account, you can browse the files in the current account.

54
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
The section content on the left side is consistent with the Closet page.

55
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
It is convenient for everyone to quickly find the files they want.

56
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Then we will load this shirt with double click.

57
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Now we will use this shirt to show you how to use the Closet app.

58
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Let's take a look at the Closet app.

59
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
First of all, I will introduce two function optimizations related to blockization.

60
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
First of all, when the customized clothing block is opened again,

61
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
you can sew it by clicking on the cutout.

62
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
When everyone is making clothes,

63
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
it is usually necessary to sew according to the cutout.

64
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
For example, the bubble sleeve in this style.

65
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,000
You can see that the cutout on the large sleeve sleeve and the sleeve on the sleeve is well sewn.

66
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Now we define the style of this bubble sleeve as the clothing block.

67
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
This is an automatic blockization label tool.

68
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:27,000
For this shirt, the part of the current automatic identification is not complete enough.

69
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
At this time, we can choose to edit the part and redefine the front part of the shirt.

70
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
The back and sleeve parts are also the same operation.

71
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
For the collar part that has been accurately identified,

72
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
we can directly choose to save the part and quickly save it.

73
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:47,000
After defining it, we can self-define it in the user,

74
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
find the option to sew by clicking on the cutout in the block.

75
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
It is a default selection.

76
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
If you cancel the selection and re-load it,

77
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
you will see that it is a cutout.

78
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:08,000
If you click on it and load the clothing block again,

79
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:14,000
you can see that it is now sewed by clicking on the cutout.

80
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
In addition, due to the fact that the parts between the styles

81
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
are usually incompatible,

82
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
in order to prevent the parts between the styles from being combined,

83
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:25,000
we can see the default selection of the module combination

84
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
to prevent the parts between the styles from being combined.

85
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
When we use the parts under the style to combine,

86
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
it can be done normally.

87
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
But when we switch to other styles to load the parts,

88
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
a warning window will appear.

89
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
This will effectively prevent the wrong parts from being combined.

90
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Now, when we convert the straight line point to a free curve point,

91
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
we can choose to keep the curve rate or tight conversion.

92
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
When choosing to keep the curve rate,

93
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
we will create multiple curve points to maintain the curve shape.

94
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
This function is the same as the previous effect.

95
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
When choosing to tight conversion,

96
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
we will not create other curve points.

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
It should be noted that such conversion

98
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:11,000
may cause the original curve shape to change.

99
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Similarly, when converting the curve point to a straight line point,

100
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
we can choose any conversion method according to our needs.

101
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,000
The two modes make the conversion method more flexible and diverse.

102
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
In the new version,

103
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,000
we can remove the interlocking relationship between the inner line and the base line on the symmetrical interlocking plate.

104
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
For example, on this shirt,

105
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
we only need to sew a small label on the left side of the large body,

106
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
then we can remove the interlocking on the inner shape on the right front piece,

107
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
and then delete it.

108
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The base line is the same.

109
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
We first remove the interlocking,

110
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
then select the base line,

111
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
then remove the interlocking,

112
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
then delete the unnecessary base line.

113
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
This function is also a long-awaited function for everyone.

114
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:57,000
I hope everyone can use it when you need it in the future.

115
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Now I want to change the circle of this shirt to a shoulder strap.

116
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
At this time, you can use the function of changing the plate.

117
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
This time, the replacement plate has also been optimized.

118
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:12,000
First of all, we can right-click on the plate that needs to be replaced.

119
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Then right-click on the plate that needs to be replaced,

120
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
and then select the plate that needs to be replaced.

121
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
This makes the replacement operation more convenient.

122
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:24,000
In addition, we can replace the plate with a number that is not consistent with the original plate.

123
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
After selecting the plate that needs to be replaced,

124
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
you will see a tool prompt.

125
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
We need to select the point that matches,

126
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
then press the return key to confirm completion.

127
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:38,000
You can see that the replacement is completed at this time.

128
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Next, we will modify the button on the shirt skirt.

129
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
In this way, you can modify the material of the button on the shirt skirt.

130
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:48,000
In 2024.2, the metal material for the button has been added to the preset.

131
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:52,000
You can use it according to your needs and select the preset you need.

132
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
This makes your operation more convenient.

133
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
This time, we have three updates on the code.

134
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:04,000
First of all, the new version supports the function of increasing the size of the code on the current code basis.

135
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
You can select the smallest size,

136
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
right-click to find it,

137
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
and insert the size at the top,

138
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
to add a smaller size.

139
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
In addition, you can use the same method

140
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
to add a new size between the two sizes.

141
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:24,000
In addition, the version also adds the function of adding a code.

142
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
You can enter the code.

143
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
When you paste the code on the board,

144
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:36,000
you can see that there is a cross mark on the corresponding position of the 2D window to indicate the location of the code.

145
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
When you switch to the edit code tool,

146
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
you can select the cross mark to enter the code.

147
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Then we will switch to different sizes to simulate and check their effects separately.

148
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Next, let's take a look at the two functions updated about the measurement points.

149
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
First of all, in 2024.2,

150
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
we have added the measurement point group function.

151
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
You can classify the measurement points through the group,

152
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:08,000
so that the information of the measurement looks clearer and more flexible.

153
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,000
The group you see now is the front and back of the costume.

154
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:17,000
You can fold up the measurement point groups that you don't need to see here.

155
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:22,000
You can also classify and rename according to your own preferences.

156
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
When a costume has multiple sizes,

157
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
in the new version,

158
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:32,000
you can hide the sizes that you don't need to see in the measurement point label.

159
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
This will make you feel more comfortable

160
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
and easier to focus on the current size.

161
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
You can also click on the icon again

162
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
to open the corresponding size display.

163
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Next, let's take a look at the two functions updated about the arrangement.

164
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
First of all, in 2024.2,

165
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
when you have selected the size that needs to be arranged,

166
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
you can choose to classify each size

167
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
and classify the arrangement according to the size.

168
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
And when you switch to the machine code,

169
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
you can distinguish the current machine code and other sizes more clearly.

170
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
In addition,

171
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:06,000
the current version also simplifies the arrangement of different colors.

172
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
The arrangement and the color are linked.

173
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,000
You can click on the color you need to arrange,

174
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
and then arrange.

175
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
When you switch to the color,

176
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:20,000
you can see that the colors of the same fabric will be arranged together.

177
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
From 2024.2,

178
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
you can adjust the chest shape of the virtual model.

179
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
In the virtual model editor,

180
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
a new editor about the chest is added,

181
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
allowing you to create a self-defined chest model.

182
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
You can adjust the shape

183
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
to make the chest closer to the round chest

184
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
or the water-bottomed chest.

185
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,000
When you need to adjust the chest again,

186
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,000
you can click on the reset button in the upper right corner

187
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
to reset the current effect.

188
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
If the shoulder is pointed towards the female model,

189
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
the chest will be bigger and wider.

190
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
The shorter the shoulder, the bigger the chest,

191
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
the wider the chest, the wider the chest,

192
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
and the height is pointed towards the female model.

193
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
The position of the breast point is high and low.

194
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
You can see this parameter more objectively

195
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
through adjustment.

196
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Next, let's take a look at the virtual model joints.

197
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
In 2024.2,

198
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
the size reduction and hiding function of the joints is supported.

199
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Open the virtual model joint.

200
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
In the adjustment window in the upper right corner,

201
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
the size adjustment has been added.

202
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
You can adjust the size of the joint to the size of your preference.

203
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
You can also reset it to the default size.

204
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
If you don't need to see a certain joint,

205
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
you can hide them in the right-click menu.

206
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
You can also right-click to display again.

207
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
In addition,

208
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
you can see that the current virtual model joint adjustment window

209
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
is also different from the previous one.

210
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
You can switch between FK and IK modes

211
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
directly in the mode area

212
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
to display the corresponding editing tool.

213
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
In 2024.2,

214
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
the function of flattening as a sheet is also optimized.

215
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
We can use this function to extract

216
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
the chest sheet drawn with a 3D drawing pen.

217
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
When you use the flattening as a sheet,

218
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
you will see that the sheet

219
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
will open the logic of the front and back sheets

220
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
in the 2D window.

221
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
In addition,

222
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
the presentation of the line direction of the sheet will be more reasonable.

223
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
After completing the basic production of the chest sheet,

224
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
when simulating and adjusting the shoulder strap of the chest,

225
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
there will often be a slip of the shoulder strap.

226
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
At this time,

227
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
we will add a fixing pin on the shoulder strap on one side.

228
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Then,

229
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
you can copy the corresponding position of the fixing pin

230
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
to the corresponding position on the corresponding sheet

231
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
to facilitate the adjustment of the shoulder strap.

232
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
In 2024.2,

233
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
we optimized the extension function of the stretch bar.

234
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
We recommend that you use the stretch bar tool

235
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
to add the stretch bar.

236
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
At this time,

237
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
you can see that different stretch areas

238
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
are distinguished by different colors,

239
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
and you can see that the arrow

240
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
is only the beginning and end of the stretch bar.

241
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Then,

242
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
you can see the attribute editor.

243
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
The extension below the stretch bar

244
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
has been added to the setting of the beginning and end.

245
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
You can set different extension effects

246
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
according to your needs here

247
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
to adjust the position where they end.

248
